WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.501
- Does anybody know
who they're voting for?

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:03.334
(all laughing)

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:04.167
Who do you think you'll vote for?

00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:05.867
Who knows, maybe I'm gonna be a snake.

00:00:05.867 --> 00:00:06.920
- Oh.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:08.480
- Welcome to "Stacks,"

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.210
the show where every vote counts.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:12.050
Today seven college students must decide

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:14.660
who gets to take home up to $2,000.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.010
The players will have
four rounds of discussion.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:20.090
After each round, there
will be blind voting.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:22.310
One gold brick equals one vote.

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:23.143
At the end of the game,

00:00:23.143 --> 00:00:26.430
the person with the tallest
stack wins the prize.

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:28.427
This is "Stacks."

00:00:28.427 --> 00:00:31.010
(upbeat music)

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.886
Hey everyone, how are
you guys feeling today?

00:00:34.886 --> 00:00:35.719
- Good.

00:00:35.719 --> 00:00:36.730
- Nervous and excited.

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:39.140
- Okay, so today's a
little special, all right?

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:40.760
So one gold brick,

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:43.350
as you can see here is worth $100

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.275
- A $100!

00:00:46.275 --> 00:00:47.108
- At the very end,

00:00:47.108 --> 00:00:49.070
depending on how many bricks
you have in your stack,

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:50.730
that's the total dollar amount

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:51.780
that you'll end up winning.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:55.770
Whoever wins could win up to $2,000.

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:56.603
- Oh my God!

00:00:56.603 --> 00:00:59.500
- Only the person with the
highest amount of bricks

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.290
is gonna take home the prize money.

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:02.210
Does that make sense?

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:03.043
- [All] Yeah.

00:01:03.043 --> 00:01:03.876
- Okay, for round one,

00:01:03.876 --> 00:01:05.750
each player will get one gold brick.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:07.160
They'll have six minutes to discuss

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.320
who they think should take the cash prize.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:11.210
Round one starts now.

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:14.400
- We should start to like
get into why you all are here

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.250
and like why you need the money

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:17.220
or why you want the money.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.840
- I'm a history major,
I'm graduating in May,

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:22.130
and so and so I'm entering the next phase.

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:24.910
And so I'll use this
money to invest in myself,

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:26.270
my mental and physical health

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:27.690
before I go into the next step

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:30.540
and then I'll use the
rest to keep myself afloat

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:32.697
as I navigate the real world.

00:01:32.697 --> 00:01:33.950
- Oh man.
(all laughing)

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:37.800
- My strategy is to be as honest
and as giving as possible,

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.960
but to also have a
little bit of skepticism.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.820
- I actually am a master's student.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:44.360
I feel like I have a decent
idea of what I want to do

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:47.360
in cinematography definitely
is it and it is expensive.

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:48.193
- Yeah.

00:01:48.193 --> 00:01:50.240
- I started developing
like a little camera kit

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.601
last semester and then
it got stolen, okay.

00:01:52.601 --> 00:01:54.000
- [All] Oh no!

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.110
- So I would love to just help
replace some of that stuff.

00:01:57.110 --> 00:01:59.330
- Definitely a portion
of it would go to my mom.

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:00.330
She's a single mother,

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:01.500
she's worked very hard

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:03.780
and she's never been
selfish with her wants.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:05.590
So truthfully, I wanna
be able to take her out

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:06.650
to a nice dinner.

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:08.130
My car insurance is coming up.

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:09.450
I wish I could give a better answer

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:11.060
but I do need to pay car insurance.

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:13.520
My biggest strategy is to
just come into the game

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.373
and be as vulnerable as I can,

00:02:15.373 --> 00:02:18.340
because I think vulnerability
is a really important step

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:20.100
in getting empathy from others

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.430
and I guess essentially

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:23.360
that's kind of what the
point of the game is.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:24.550
- I think that's totally valid.

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:28.050
I feel like I put my needs over
my wants way too many times

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:30.160
and sometimes it's because
I think people like

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:31.700
tell me that I don't deserve it.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:35.010
So it's like I wanna use
the money to spend it on

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:35.843
things that I want

00:02:35.843 --> 00:02:38.010
and things that will
make me like be happier

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:40.230
and live a better like
fulfillment in life.

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:41.500
- My mom's also a single mother.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:42.640
She actually just gave birth

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:45.010
to her fourth kid in the summer 15

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:48.520
which I've been taking care
of while doing online school.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.637
So I live in Burbank and I go to UCI

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:52.430
and so that's like four hours.

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:54.310
I also have like a hospital bill

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:56.590
that I'm trying to like get
off already and over with.

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:58.670
And after hearing the amount
that we might be winning,

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:00.450
I feel like that would benefit me a lot

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:02.275
to just getting that out of the way.

00:03:02.275 --> 00:03:03.108
- Yeah.
(all laughing)

00:03:03.108 --> 00:03:04.510
- I don't know, I would
use the money towards a car

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:06.200
because that's like kind of
one of the biggest things.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.820
I'm not able to work
as much as I should be

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:10.920
because I need a car to get around,

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.370
and public transportation doesn't go

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:13.630
as far as I need to work.

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:15.770
- I have a really good
shot of getting into UCLA,

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:17.460
but I still might not be able to go.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:18.910
And that's just the reality of things,

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:21.590
is because it's so
expensive to live in LA.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:23.640
It's really sad to see everything you've

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.460
tried to work hard, not pay off.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:26.293
- [All] Yeah.

00:03:26.293 --> 00:03:29.130
- So I'm trying to save
every penny that I have

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:31.963
that I get from my $15
an hour part-time job.

00:03:31.963 --> 00:03:33.862
(machine chinks)

00:03:33.862 --> 00:03:34.960
- Shout out minimum wage.

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:37.223
- Does anybody know
who they're voting for?

00:03:37.223 --> 00:03:38.143
(all laughing)

00:03:38.143 --> 00:03:40.210
I mean, you don't wanna
disclose that, you don't.

00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:41.392
- Who do you think you'll vote for?

00:03:41.392 --> 00:03:42.880
- Yeah, who are you voting for?

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:44.960
- Honestly, I was really touched

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:47.230
by Destiny's story and her situation.

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:49.121
So I might vote for her.

00:03:49.121 --> 00:03:49.954
- Facts, I'm voting for you.

00:03:49.954 --> 00:03:50.787
- Throwing that out there.

00:03:50.787 --> 00:03:51.620
- Yeah.
- Yes.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:52.670
- But who knows?

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:53.530
Maybe I'm gonna be a snake.

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:54.660
No, I'm just kidding.

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:56.278
I'm just kidding, I'm sorry.

00:03:56.278 --> 00:03:57.160
- This is a lot harder

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:58.122
than I thought it was gonna be--

00:03:58.122 --> 00:03:59.080
- It's really hard.

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:00.956
- Like vote for really good reasons

00:04:00.956 --> 00:04:02.090
- But it's just the first round.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:03.170
And like one thing that we need to know

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:04.610
is like these are our worst problems.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.580
And like, just because one
seems worse than the other

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.400
doesn't mean that they're
not valid, you know.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:09.390
- Yeah, 100%

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:10.730
- We could all use the $2,000.

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:11.660
- Time is up.

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:12.690
Thought also, thank you so much

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:14.240
for sharing all of your stories.

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:15.770
I feel like that was really nice to hear.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:17.211
We'll see if anyone's lying.

00:04:17.211 --> 00:04:18.300
(all laughing)

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:19.620
It's time to vote.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:20.690
Each player will vote

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:23.100
for who they think should win the prize,

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.330
but there's a catch.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.530
If all seven players vote for themselves,

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:29.621
the game is over and no one wins.

00:04:29.621 --> 00:04:32.450
(suspenseful music)

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:34.560
- I know commuting to
school is really hard

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:37.180
and hospital bills can
be really expensive.

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:39.904
So I think she deserves it the most.

00:04:39.904 --> 00:04:42.904
(suspenseful music)

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:54.960
- I felt like we had a very similar case

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:57.060
and I would rather not for myself.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:58.472
I would rather vote for her.

00:04:58.472 --> 00:05:01.472
(suspenseful music)

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:11.162
- Because of the rule that
we may lose everything,

00:05:11.162 --> 00:05:14.711
but it was a risk that
I'm willing to take.

00:05:14.711 --> 00:05:17.294
(gentle music)

00:05:21.974 --> 00:05:24.660
- So Charlie already said he
was gonna vote for Destiny,

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:28.587
so that's telling me that
I can vote for myself.

00:05:28.587 --> 00:05:31.170
(gentle music)

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:33.590
- I chose destiny

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:35.930
because I was in a really
similar position to her

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:37.260
when I was a freshman,

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:38.980
and I understand how hard it can be

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:40.190
commuting so far from school,

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:43.383
so hopefully the vote will
help her out in some way.

00:05:43.383 --> 00:05:45.966
(gentle music)

00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:51.890
- I was moved the most by
Destiny and Miyeong's stories.

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:54.470
I wonder why Charlie tried to curry favor

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:55.547
with Destiny though.

00:05:56.397 --> 00:05:58.980
(gentle music)

00:06:02.366 --> 00:06:03.199
- No.

00:06:03.199 --> 00:06:04.922
- I'm keeping you in suspense.

00:06:04.922 --> 00:06:06.424
- No.

00:06:06.424 --> 00:06:09.878
- Three, two, one open.

00:06:09.878 --> 00:06:12.313
(gentle music)

00:06:12.313 --> 00:06:13.146
(all surprises)

00:06:13.146 --> 00:06:14.720
- Nice, yes.
- Tada!

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:18.310
- Like money triggers
such a primal instinct,

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:19.900
especially seeing like no bricks

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:22.020
on my pile the first round,

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:22.990
it kind of hurt me a little bit,

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:24.830
but I realized that it
was all coming from that

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:27.940
sort of innate instinct that
like I deserve this money.

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:29.955
- Destiny, you're killing it right now.

00:06:29.955 --> 00:06:31.649
(gentle music)

00:06:31.649 --> 00:06:33.890
(bricks clinking)

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:36.450
In round two only players
who currently have stacks

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:38.750
will receive two more
gold bricks for voting,

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:41.860
but all players can
participate in the discussion.

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:43.210
So if you don't have a brick,

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:45.390
try to convince those who do, begin.

00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:46.730
- This is capitalism.

00:06:46.730 --> 00:06:48.190
- This is...
(all laughing)

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:49.320
- We should sort of spend it on the time

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:50.940
that people don't have bricks.

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:51.943
- I agree.

00:06:51.943 --> 00:06:52.810
- I agree with that.

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:55.280
- I disagree, and let me say why.

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:57.150
Because they're setting up the game

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.450
where we're supposed to try to advocate

00:06:58.450 --> 00:06:59.410
for the people who don't have bricks,

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:01.080
but in the end the person who wins

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:02.960
only gets the amount of
bricks that we give them.

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:04.090
Right now Destiny's in the lead,

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:06.600
Destiny's gonna get my every
brick for the rest of the game.

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:08.580
I'd rather have somebody have their life

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:10.380
really changed and affected,

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:13.160
than have a lot of bricks
spread out for a lot of people.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.003
- Here's my thing with the bricks

00:07:14.003 --> 00:07:15.980
because I agree with what you're saying,

00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:18.330
but the also the more bricks that we have,

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:20.190
the more bricks that are
gonna be distributed.

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:21.480
That means that there's
more money all around

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:22.340
and then we can put more money

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:24.820
into whatever person we
want to win, you know?

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:26.120
- So maybe we should start with the people

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:28.540
without bricks first and
then move to the second round

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:30.560
just because I feel like
we're running out of time.

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:32.089
- [All] Yeah.

00:07:32.089 --> 00:07:33.950
- Lets start without the bar.

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:36.900
- I'd like to maybe invest
in some hearing aids

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:39.480
or do something about my jaw

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:41.290
which has been hurting me a lot recently.

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:43.290
- You didn't vote for yourself, right?

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:44.780
Why didn't you vote for yourself?

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:48.513
- Well, I would like to be
in the spirit of giving.

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:50.691
- I like that attitude.

00:07:50.691 --> 00:07:51.740
(all laughing)

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:53.830
- Yeah, so to give more
context to my situation,

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:56.480
my mom has been on survival
mode her whole life.

00:07:56.480 --> 00:07:58.170
She got the chance to
reconnect with my dad.

00:07:58.170 --> 00:07:59.970
He passed away shortly thereafter,

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:02.870
so that kind of light
was taken away from her.

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:04.470
I would take that money and use it

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:05.560
to maybe take her out

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:07.610
where she won't have to worry at all about

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:08.920
any financial repercussion.

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:12.240
So I can bring that light
back in her a little bit.

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:13.460
- I think it's interesting how

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:16.130
a lot of us that now
haven't voted for ourselves

00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:18.470
are now like wanting that money.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:20.950
So it's interesting to
see how that changed.

00:08:20.950 --> 00:08:22.900
Who voted for themselves, I'm curious.

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:23.733
Did anybody vote for themselves?

00:08:23.733 --> 00:08:24.566
- There's no shame in that everyone.

00:08:24.566 --> 00:08:25.548
- There's no shame.

00:08:25.548 --> 00:08:26.770
(upbeat music)

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:28.050
- I know I have a brick on mine,

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:28.920
but I voted for Destiny.

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:30.260
- I voted for you.

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:31.690
- Oh my God.

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:33.200
- I wanna know what people
with bricks are thinking

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:34.235
in terms of like,

00:08:34.235 --> 00:08:35.068
do you think you'll split your vote

00:08:35.068 --> 00:08:36.790
or do you think that you'll
give them all to one person?

00:08:36.790 --> 00:08:38.720
- I definitely wanna split it.

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:40.430
- I am also thinking about splitting mine,

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:41.970
it just feels fair

00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:44.330
to help even the playing
field a little bit.

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:45.410
- It worries me a little bit.

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:48.010
I'd rather have somebody get
as much money as possible.

00:08:48.010 --> 00:08:49.890
The person who has the
most bricks is gonna win.

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:52.020
So either we can all band together

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:53.610
and really change someone's life

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:55.530
by giving them the most money possible,

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:57.240
or we can just for the sake of sympathy,

00:08:57.240 --> 00:08:58.880
give people bricks that
don't mean anything.

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:00.270
So I was surprised when other people

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:02.340
didn't see that same strategy right away.

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:03.380
My perspective's changed a lot.

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:05.800
I don't know if I really
want the money anymore.

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:08.080
Just because I don't wanna try to compete

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:09.120
and have somebody just lose out

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:10.400
on something they could be getting to.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:13.110
So I know that I'm putting
all my bricks for Destiny.

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:14.010
- It's such a hard dilemma,

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:15.780
like one part of me
really wants the money,

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:17.343
and the other part of me is like,

00:09:17.343 --> 00:09:20.270
but that is like a really big
problem in somebody's life.

00:09:20.270 --> 00:09:21.976
And like this will really benefit them.

00:09:21.976 --> 00:09:22.809
(gentle music)

00:09:22.809 --> 00:09:23.642
- For this round,

00:09:23.642 --> 00:09:24.810
players can use their two gold bricks

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:26.190
to vote for any player,

